  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support Towards Durable Solutions for People Displaced by Tropical Cyclone Freddy.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tropical Cyclone (TC) Freddy made landfall in Malawi in March 2023 and despite early warning communication at all levels, it turned out to be one of the worst cyclones in Malawi&#x2019;s history to date, with heavy rains causing multiple flood events and landslides across 16 districts. 
 
Through this project, IOM is contributing to safe and dignified living conditions for displaced populations affected by Cyclone Freddy and supporting them in attaining durable solutions through Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM), Shelter and Non-Food Items (NFI), and Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) within the context of addressing disaster displacement and strengthening resilience to future shocks.</narrative>
  </description>
